 "notes": "Curve is the Experiment B (measured) 95% C.L. exclusion on the UDM-photon coupling g_gamma from Fig. 2(a), Galactic-halo scenario, extracted from the vector PDF (exclusions.pdf); axis calibration verified against tick marks and against Eq. (5) with the delta-f/f limits of Fig. 1. Paper convention alpha(t)=alpha_0[1+g_gamma*phi] with g_gamma in eV^-1; converted to Damour-Donoghue d_e = g_gamma/kappa, kappa = sqrt(4pi)/(1.22e19 GeV), i.e. d_e = g_gamma[eV^-1] x 3.4416e27 eV. The paper also bounds the electron coupling g_e (Fig. 2a top, only above 50 kHz) and d_me (Fig. 3); the photon coupling covers the full investigated mass range 8e-11 - 4e-7 eV and is reported here. Experiment A curves are 'ultimate apparatus sensitivity' (not a valid exclusion due to unexcluded spurious peaks) and are excluded; Solar/Earth-halo scenario panels also not used. rho_DM = 3e-6 eV^4 ~ 0.39 GeV/cm^3 assumed by the paper.",
